  "reason": "The change fixes the root cause described in the bug report. The bug occurred because ratio columns were being squeezed narrower than their content width plus padding, causing content to disappear. By using `width_ranges[columns.index(column)].maximum` (the measured content width) instead of `column.width or 1` (which defaults to 1 for ratio columns), ratio columns now maintain a minimum width based on their actual content needs. This ensures that in the example `table.add_row('a', 'b', 'cccccccccccccccc')` with ratios 1:1:10 at width 14, the columns with 'a' and 'b' will not be squeezed below the width needed to display their content plus padding."
